        <div id="choose" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. How Do You Choose the Right Mattress?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Start with how you sleep, not with brands. The position you wake up in most mornings decides how much a mattress needs to cushion your shoulders and hips versus how much it needs to hold your spine level. Side sleepers need give at the shoulder and hip. Back sleepers need support under the lower back. Stomach sleepers need a surface firm enough that the hips do not sink and bend the spine.
          </p>

          <p>
            Next comes body weight, because firmness is relative. A mattress the maker calls medium-firm feels firm to someone who weighs 130 pounds and close to medium to someone who weighs 250. Heavier sleepers also compress comfort foam faster, so they need thicker support layers and denser foam to avoid early sagging.
          </p>

          <p>
            The third question is heat. All-foam beds, and memory foam in particular, hold more body heat than hybrids, whose coil layer lets air move. If you wake up sweating, lean toward a hybrid or a foam bed with a breathable cover and a cooling top layer.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">The short version</h3>

          <p>
            If you share a bed, sleep in more than one position, or simply do not know, a medium-firm hybrid is the safest default. It is the feel most of our picks share, and it is the one owners most often describe as neither too hard nor too soft. The rest of this guide explains when to deviate from it, and the specialist guides cover each case in depth: <a href="/best-mattress-for-side-sleepers/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-bold no-underline hover:underline">mattresses for side sleepers</a>, <a href="/best-mattress-for-seniors/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-bold no-underline hover:underline">mattresses for seniors</a>, and <a href="/best-mattress-topper/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-bold no-underline hover:underline">mattress toppers</a> for fixing a bed you already own.
          </p>
        </div>

