            10. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Judging a mattress on the first night</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Foam needs time to expand and soften, and your body needs time to adjust. Many people return a bed that would have suited them after a month. Sleep on it for three to four weeks before deciding, and note the minimum-keep period in the trial terms.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying firm because it sounds healthy</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Firmer is not automatically better for your back. Side sleepers on a firm bed often get shoulder and hip pain, and lighter sleepers may not compress a firm bed at all. Match firmness to your position and weight, not to a general idea of support.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring your body weight</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Firmness ratings assume an average sleeper. Heavier people experience every bed as softer and wear comfort foam faster, while lighter people find the same bed firmer. Adjust one step firmer or softer from the position guidance to account for your weight.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Putting a new mattress on an old foundation</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A sagging box spring or widely spaced slats will make a new mattress dip and can void the warranty. Check the maker's foundation requirements, and replace a worn base at the same time as the mattress.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Skipping the mattress protector</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Most warranties are voided by stains, and sweat and spills break down foam. A waterproof, breathable protector costs a fraction of the mattress and keeps both the bed and the warranty intact.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

