        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the top rated mattress type for most people?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                A medium-firm hybrid suits the widest range of sleepers. Its coils give support, bounce and airflow, and its foam layers relieve pressure at the shoulders and hips. It works for back sleepers, most side sleepers and couples. Side sleepers who want more cushioning, and hot sleepers, may prefer a softer hybrid or a latex bed.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How long should a mattress last?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Most well-made mattresses last seven to ten years. Budget all-foam beds can soften within three to five years, especially under heavier sleepers. Replace a mattress when it has visible sagging, when you wake up stiff and feel better elsewhere, or when it has passed the warranty's sag depth.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Are mattress in a box beds any good?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Yes. Rolling and compression do not harm well-made foam or pocketed coils, and online brands save money on showrooms. The main differences are the long home trial, which is a better test than lying on a bed in a store, and a day or two of expansion and off-gassing.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What firmness is best for back pain?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Medium-firm is the most common recommendation, because it supports the lower back while letting the hips and shoulders settle enough to keep the spine straight. Very soft beds let the hips sag and very firm beds create pressure points. Persistent back pain is worth discussing with a doctor or physical therapist.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Should couples get a hybrid or memory foam mattress?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Memory foam isolates motion best, so it suits couples where one partner is a light sleeper. Hybrids with pocketed coils still isolate motion well while adding bounce, edge support and airflow, and they handle two different body weights better. For most couples a hybrid is the better all-round choice.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Do I need a box spring for a new mattress?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Usually not. Most modern mattresses need a firm, flat base such as a platform bed, a slatted frame with slats close together, or a foundation, not a traditional box spring with springs inside. Check the maker's requirements, because an unsupported base can cause sagging and void the warranty.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">When is the best time to buy a mattress?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Online mattress brands run their deepest discounts around major holidays, including Presidents Day, Memorial Day, Labor Day and Black Friday. Many beds are discounted most of the year, so compare the actual sale price between brands rather than the percentage off, and buy when your current bed is failing.
              </p>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>

